update investigationfinding
set findingcomments ='The Department received reported concerns for 15-year-old Ali overdosing for the second time on Percocet. Reported concerns also for Ali using other drugs as well. Reportedly, Mr. and Mrs. Vitija have not gotten needed services for Ali due to his suspected substance use.',
omissiondesc = 'Jehona Vitija, Biological mother and caregiver.',
isharmsubstantial =1,
harmdesc = 'Through the investigation the Department corroborated that Ali was taken to Meritus Medical Center (MMC) for a Percocet overdose and this was not the first time. Mr. Vitija confirmed that MMC provided the family with SUD treatment providers locally however he had not scheduled an intake appointment for Ali. Worker observed Ali to have signs and symptoms of substance use, such as pale skin, sweating, paranoia, inability to sit still, pinned pupils, and agitation. The Department received reported concerns for Ali losing a substantial amount of weight in a short period of time which was corroborated by Ali himself. Ali stated that the weight loss was from his getting fit however the presence of the addiction symptoms correlates with substance usage. According to MMC records, Ali has been treated for an overdose of narcotics on multiple occasions. Mr. and Mrs. Vitija shared that they have noticed the changes in Ali as well. According to the National Institute of Health, opioid misuse can cause unintentional injury and death. According to Youth.gov, family involvement in adolescent opioid addiction treatment is crucial to a successful recovery. Due to the corroborating medical evidence, the lack of substance use treatment engagement, and the admission from both parents that Ali has been using substances this case will be INDICATED',
updatedby='CJAMS-66528',
updatedon=now()
where  investigationfindingid ='61d970ce-1460-4321-af1d-8f71b69e0e98';

