--JEHONA VITIJA
update investigationallegation
set activeflag=1,
victim_explanation='Worker met with Ali in his bedroom. Ali paced the entire time and looked out the window on multiple occasions. Workerinquired about substances. Ali strongly denied using any substances. Worker inquired about Percocet usage however Alidenied using them. Worker informed Ali that worker knows that he was at Meritus Medical Center recently for Percocetoverdose and he stated that he was just tired. Ali stated, “I’m not addicted.” Worker informed Ali that worker neveraccused him of being addicted. Worker was inquiring about Ali’s recent visit to Meritus Medical Center. Worker inquiredabout Ali’s last use of any substances. Ali denied using and stated, “I don’t take anything.” Worker inquired about Ali’sperspective on his family. Ali vented that his mom needs to take responsibility for how she treated them when they wereyounger. Worker inquired about Ali’s friends. Ali stated that he has friends in school, however he refused to talk aboutthem. Ali’s room appeared to have a queen size bed, dresser with no drawers, TV, and closet with clothes. Thereappeared to be new flooring boxes in Ali’s room as well. No safety concerns were noted with Ali’s room.',
sibling_explanation='Worker met with Emine in her bedroom alone. Worker inquired about Emine’s perspective of her family. Emine sharedthat she loves her family and her mom but there has to be changes. She shared that her parents don’t say anything to Aliat all. She vented how she feels that her parents always take things out on her when they need to focus on Ali. Sheshared that her grades are not good because of what’s going on at her house. Emine vented her frustration for Ali andhis behaviors as he will argue with his parents or do things to get his way. She shared that Ali will bug her even after shetells him to leave her alone. Emine shared that she used to go to a counselor, but he was a male and she didn’t “click”with him. Emine shared at first that she would be willing to go back to therapy if she had a female, but then stated, “I’malright.” Emine acknowledged that she does leave without permission, but she needs to get away from the house. Eminedenied using substances, however she did not want to talk about the subject. Emine shared that when she hung out atthe Fairgrounds with her friends, she hung out with a guy but didn’t tell her parents. She stated that her parents don’twant her hanging out with guys. Emine stated that she was hanging out with boys from her school. Emine cried duringthe conversation and stated that she wants her family better and to have a relationship with her mom. Emine’s room has abed, dresser, and desk. She has a closet full of clothes. There were personal items and clothes all over the floor, but nosafety concerns. Halil was quiet and shy. He did not want to speak with worker.',
guardian_explanation='See alleged maltreator''s explanation.',
maltreator_explanation='Mrs. Vitija shared that she got a call from her daughter asking her to check on Ali because he wasn''t answering her texts. Mr. Vitija shared that his wife called him at work, and he met them at the hospital. Mr. Vitija shared that he has lived in Hagerstown for years and had to GPS how to get to the hospital because he''s never been there. Ali and Emine escalated stating that they do not have problems or use substances. Ali stated, “I''m fine, ma’am.” 

Mrs. Vitija explained that the children do not listen to her, so she leaves it up to Mr. Vitija to discipline them. Mrs. Vitija stated that her teenage children tell her that they do not have to listen to her. She shared that her children call her all kinds of names and she has no control over Ali and Emine. 

Mr. Vitija shared that he works all the time to pay the bills, so he is not home. He shared that he gets little sleep because Ali and Emine are always leaving or doing things that they are not supposed to. Mr. Vitija stated that he is always getting calls from the school to pick Ali up. He stated that he has to pick Ali up today because Ali was pacing and disrupting the class. He shared that Ali leaves the house fine and then somehow in between the time Ali leaves the house until he goes to school, Ali gets substances. Mr. Vitija shared that he or Mrs. Vitija do not give him drugs but somehow Ali gets them. 

Mrs. Vitija shared that they have three older children that are not living in the home as they are adults now. She shared that one of her adult daughters uses substances and she used to be close with Ali. Mrs. Vitija shared that she is not sure if her older daughter gave Ali anything. Mrs. Vitija shared that Emine will leave at all hours and stay out without permission. She shared that the other weekend Emine had a friend over who wasn''t supposed to be at her house (Mrs. Vitija didn''t want anyone over) but Emine brought her over anyway. The friend was “mouthing off” to her and all she wanted was to let the girl''s mom know that she was at their house. 

Worker inquired about substance usage with Emine and Ali. Mr. Vitija shared that he has no idea where or what the kids are taking. He shared that Ali leaves home fine and he is not sure what happens between home and school. He shared that he is concerned for his children. He vented his frustration on how the kids have changed and now use bad language and are disrespectful. Mr. Vitija reported that COVID really hurt their family. He shared that he noticed a downfall during COVID. Mr. Vitija shared that he has noticed that his family likes to leave when things get tough. He stated that Mrs. Vitija went to Miami for a week last year when things got rough. He shared that he called and asked her to come home. Mr. Vitija stated that Emine and Ali started acting out really bad and will leave without permission when they get upset. Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija shared that their marriage is not good either. Worker explained that from the Department perspective the family is in need of services, more than just marriage help.

Worker provided a discussion on the safety and well-being of the children. Worker provided information regarding concerns for Ali and his substance use. Worker informed both parents that Ali''s presentation right now shows that he may be under the influence of a substance. Worker explained that Ali is pacing, sweating, dark circles, and Ali''s hand shook as he took a drink of his water. Worker provided the number for Mobile Crisis. Worker also informed the family that they need to use Meritus Medical Center''s ED if Ali escalates. Worker informed the family that Ali and Emine both needs substance use evaluations and if needed, treatment. Worker informed the family that there needs to mental health evaluations for all of them. Worker discussed that the family would benefit from family therapy.

Worker discussed the possibility that Emine and Ali not being willing to partake in substance use evaluations and treatment as well as mental health services. Worker explained that the family need to file for Children In Need of Supervision through the courts. Worker explained that the Department is able to transfer the family''s case to the Family Preservation Department as the family needs a lot of assistance. Worker explained that Family Preservation is voluntary and explained the services. Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija were both willing to voluntarily partake in Family Preservation.

During the conversation with Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija, Ali kept walking out of his room and stating that his parents are lying. Ali appeared very paranoid. 

Mr. Vitija expressed his concerns for getting treatment for his children, especially Ali, and the treatment doing more harm than good. He shared that he is worried that treatment would “mess” Ali up worse than what he is. Worker explained that Mr. Vitija that he will be held accountable for his actions if he doesn''t get Ali help. Worker explained worker''s observation and informed Mr. Vitija that his children and family need further interventions. Worker explained that if Mr. Vitija does not do what is needed for his family then he could face an investigation through the Department and eventually the Department could step in and obtain court order for the family to participate in services. Mrs. Vitija was immediately agreeable. Mr. Vitija shared that he is concerned for his family and agreed to services. 

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
Worker completed a scheduled home visit with Mrs. Vitija, Mr. Vitija, Ali, Emine, and Halil for a warm hand-off with Family Preservation worker, Amber Anderson. Upon arrival, worker observed the small window on the right side of the door frame had been replaced. Mrs. Vitija answered the door and shared that Mr. Vitija was in the back yard and she would get them. Worker inquired about worker''s shoes and asked if Mrs. Vitija would like worker to remove worker''s shoes. Mrs. Vitija shared that Mr. Vitija would probably want worker to remove shoes therefore worker did so. When worker arrived, worker received a text message from Amber stating that she was handling a personal event as her car was hit. Amber shared that she would get back to worker.

 Mrs. Vitija welcomed worker to sit in the dining room while she continued to get Mr. Vitija to speak with worker. When worker walked into the kitchen Ali and Emine came out of their rooms and to the kitchen. Both teens asked worker why worker was there as they didn''t know that worker was coming. Worker explained to both youth that worker was there to meet with them and was to have them meet their new worker for continuing services. Emine stated, "well my family is fine, and we don''t need your help." Worker politely explained that the family would benefit from continuing services and their parents agreed therefore continuation will happen. Ali reiterated what Emine stated however did not engage as they appeared to both start to escalate. 
 
 Mr. Vitija came inside and apologized for not being inside when worker showed, and worker reassured him that it was okay. Mr. Vitija asked worker to sit outside as it was nice out and he had more freedom to speak without the older two youth interfering. Worker agreed and went outside with Mr. and Mrs. Vitija. Halil as in the living room watching TV insight of both parents as they sat looking into the home on the back deck. Emine and Ali both came to the sliding glass door telling their parents do not talk about them that they were fine. Worker informed Emine that worker is aware of her going to HPD yesterday with her friend after leaving her home. Worker also informed Ali that worker knew that he left last night and took their neighbor''s car. Both youths were surprised that worker knew that these events had taken place. Emine and Ali retreated inside without argument. 
 
 Mr. Vitija shared that since worker was there last, he has come to the realization that his home may not be the best fit for Ali and Emine. Worker explored for further detail. Mr. Vitija shared that Ali has not seemed to be as bad as when he had to go to the hospital, but he is still having trouble. Mr. Vitija expressed his frustration for Ali taking the neighbors car last night without permission. He shared that Emine also leaves at all hours of the night and day without asking. He shared that he feels that Emine is hanging out with the wrong people and is afraid that she may be using substances, too. Mr. Vitija commented that he has thought about sending Ali and Emine back to Albanian to family that he has there due to their behaviors here in the United States. He shared that at least in Albania, they would be more respectful to the family. Mr. Vitija shared that he has tried to set rules for Ali and Emine to follow but they don''t listen and are always breaking boundaries. 
 
 Mrs. Vitija was surprised by this information that Mr. Vitija provided about sending the children back to Albania. Mrs. Vitija shared that she would be okay with this as she feels her children would be better off in Albania. Mrs. Vitija expressed her desire to get a divorce from Mr. Vitija due to him not listening, lack of communication between the two, and their marriage "being over for years." Mrs. Vitija expressed her frustration that Mr. Vitija plays the nice guy however he pits the children against her. She shared that when they fight, Mr. Vitija says stuff loud enough for the kids to hear despite arguing in private. Mrs. Vitija shared that she has asked to go for a drive to work out their differences many times, but Mr. Vitija refuses. She shared that Mr. Vitija will tell the kids their problems which doesn''t help their respect for her. She shared that this also makes the children feel that they can tell her what to do and try to make decisions for themselves without asking them first. Mrs. Vitija shared that she now works night shift and three days a week. She reported that she would like to get her own place or even live in the same house with Mr. Vitija so Halil could still have his parents, but they work opposite shifts.
 
 Worker explored Mrs. Vitija bringing up divorce. Mrs. Vitija shared that she and Mr. Vitija both know that this discussion was coming and should have been done a long time ago. She shared that she there is so many issues and nothing seems to get better. Mrs. Vitija vented about Mr. Vitija not wanting her to visit her family. Mr. Vitija vented that at a family gathering years ago, Mrs. Vitija''s brothers beat him up in his own home so of course he doesn''t want them in his home. He shared that he opened his home and welcomed them to eat his food and make his home like their own and then they did that to him. He shared that he has every right now to allow them in his home. 
 
 Mr. Vitija did not provide much about how he was feeling about hearing divorce but did not deny that the relationship is damaged. Worker encouraged that the family seek marital counseling as well as individual and family counseling. Worker informed both Mrs. Vitija and Mr. Vitija that the family will need to have goals when working with the Family Preservation worker, Amber. Worker explained that the Department has already set goals such as SUD evaluations for Ali and Emine; MH evaluations for the entire family; parenting education; routine and structure. However, it would be beneficial for the both of them to have goals in mind to help their family and martial/family counseling is a goal. 
 
 After Mrs. Vitija shared her desire for a divorce, she appeared to be freer and like a weight was lifted off her shoulders. Mrs. Vitija smiled more and seemed to speak more openly about the issues in the family. Mrs. Vitija shared that one of their older daughters called her recently asking for help and telling her that she was pregnant. Mrs. Vitija shared that she would like to help her daughter. Mr. Vitija started to object, however worker interjected and reminded Mr. Vitija that the conversation regarding their oldest can be held between the two later. 
 
 Worker discussed increasing the case to an Investigation instead of an Alternative Response due to the concerns that this is the second overdose for Ali. Worker explained that after the first overdose Ali should have been engaged in an SUD program however he was not and now there has been a second overdose Worker informed both parents that worker understands the hesitation of putting Ali into treatment due to the possibility of negative effects, however allowing Ali to continue on the path he is on will eventually lead to him making a choice that is not reversible. Worker provided more education around the effects of substance use on teens as well as the dangers as it could be fatal. Worker explained that the family needs to take this serious as Emine is now possibly using. Worker explained that the family has an obligation to ensure the safety and well-being of their children. 
 
 Worker informed both parents that Amber did respond to worker stating that she was unable to make the home visit but would call them and schedule. Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija were very understanding and agreed that it was okay. Both ensured that Amber was safe. 
 
 Worker reiterated that worker is transferring the case to Amber and she will work through their goals. Worker went over the recommendations from the Department, i.e. SUD evals, MH evals, parenting education, structure, etc. Worker informed both parents that they were given the information for SUD eval providers in the area and they have not reached out to any. Worker explained the importance of getting the youth in for evaluations as soon as possible. 
 
 Worker answered all questions that Mr. and Mrs. Vitija had. While worker was walking out of the home, Ali and Emine appeared to have some paranoia asking worker and the Vitija''s if we talked about them. Worker explained to both youth that the conversation revolved around the family as a whole. Worker explained that the adult issues are between adults, however there are things that the Department is going to help the family with. Both youth stated that they are fine and their family is fine. Worker explained to both of the youth that the Department has placed services into their home due to concerns. 
 
 As worker was walking out, Mr. Vitija walked worker to worker''s car. Mr. Vitija shared that he is going to apologize to the neighbor because Ali took their car. He shared his frustration that Ali and his female friend (both same age) took her parents car. He shared that in his country the parents should take responsibly for their child''s actions or it looks like they are weak. Worker explained that in that same thought pattern, Mr. Vitija should be taking responsibility for Ali''s overdoses and not seeking outside help. Worker again explained that Ali has a problem that cannot be fix without intervention of professionals and there''s concern that Emine may be the same way. Mr. Vitija agreed to make changes necessary for his family.',
med_assessmnts='Reported concerns for Ali being taken to Meritus Medical Center for Percocet overdose.',
expert_assessmnts='N/A',
collateral_interviews='Worker phoned Ofc. Morris regarding Emine. Ofc. Morris shared that the dad finally showed up 2 1/2 hours later and heis not satisfied with the dad. Ofc. Morris shared that Emine left on Sunday or more Saturday evening with her friends.She went with friends to visit other friends in Hagerstown. He shared that these friends sound to be much older but Emineor her friend would not give any detail about their friends. One of the friends was supposed to give both girls a ride butthe friend kicked both girls out. Emine and her friend walked to HPD around 11:00 am. The friend''s mom picked her upwithin 9 minutes, but they had to call Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija multiple times. They had to send a Deputy to Mr. Vitija''shome to get someone to come. Ofc. Gladden finally got a hold of Mr. Vitija and Mr. Vitija stated they can keep Emine andhe would get there when he got there. Emine told both Officers that she is not cared for or loved at home and no onecares that she is home. Ofc. Morris shared that it does not sound like Emine is in a good environment. Ofc. Morrisrequested that the Department help Emine get into mental health treatment. She told him that she was in mental healthtreatment before but her mom refused to take her to the appointments. Ofc. Morris tried to get Emine to talk with theirCIT (crisis unit) but Emine refused. He shared that Emine appears to have significant trauma. Worker reassured Ofc.Morris and Ofc. Gladden that the Department will make every effort to link the family to services. Report #24005510',
criminal_history_inv='According to MD Case Search, Mrs. Vitija has was found guilty in 11/2023 for an unattended child and placed on PBJ.According to MD Case Search, Mr. Vitija does not have any criminal history',
home_conditions='The home was observed to be safe for the youth in the home.',
law_enforcement_inv='There is no law enforcement involvement at this time.',
updatedby='CJAMS-66528',
updatedon=now()
where investigationallegationid='67d86839-c194-4abd-a730-86dfed69456d';

--Nexhat Vitija
