collateral_interviews='Worker phoned Ofc. Morris regarding Emine. Ofc. Morris shared that the dad finally showed up 2 1/2 hours later and heis not satisfied with the dad. Ofc. Morris shared that Emine left on Sunday or more Saturday evening with her friends.She went with friends to visit other friends in Hagerstown. He shared that these friends sound to be much older but Emineor her friend would not give any detail about their friends. One of the friends was supposed to give both girls a ride butthe friend kicked both girls out. Emine and her friend walked to HPD around 11:00 am. The friends mom picked her upwithin 9 minutes, but they had to call Mr. Vitija and Mrs. Vitija multiple times. They had to send a Deputy to Mr. Vitija''shome to get someone to come. Ofc. Gladden finally got a hold of Mr. Vitija and Mr. Vitija stated they can keep Emine andhe would get there when he got there. Emine told both Officers that she is not cared for or loved at home and no onecares that she is home. Ofc. Morris shared that it doesn''t sound like Emine is in a good environment. Ofc. Morrisrequested that the Department help Emine get into mental health treatment. She told him that she was in mental healthtreatment before but her mom refused to take her to the appointments. Ofc. Morris tried to get Emine to talk with theirCIT (crisis unit) but Emine refused. He shared that Emine appears to have significant trauma. Worker reassured Ofc. Morris and Ofc. Gladden that the Department will make every effort to link the family to services. Report #24005510',
